WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.892
Threat actor profiles can draw from many evidence sources.

2
00:00:03.892 --> 00:00:26.541
Internal security telemetry, incident reports, phishing reports, infrastructure indicators, malware analysis summaries at a high level, vulnerability exploitation reports at a high level, threat intelligence reports, vendor intelligence, government advisories, open-source reporting, and historical case notes can all contribute.

3
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:34.636
Each source should be evaluated for reliability, freshness, relevance, and whether it is authorized for the intended use.

4
00:00:34.636 --> 00:00:40.707
Source provenance is the evidence trail behind a claim, observation, or analytic judgment.

5
00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:51.448
A profile should make it possible to trace important statements back to the report, telemetry summary, incident note, advisory, or case record that supports them.

6
00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:55.496
AI-generated claims should keep those references attached.

7
00:00:55.496 --> 00:01:00.788
Without provenance, a profile can become a polished story that no one can verify.

8
00:01:00.788 --> 00:01:04.602
Preparing data for AI summarization requires restraint.

9
00:01:04.602 --> 00:01:12.931
Analysts should provide the model enough context to perform the task, but avoid exposing unnecessary sensitive information.

10
00:01:12.931 --> 00:01:27.563
Internal hostnames, personal data, customer information, private communications, sensitive incident details, and raw telemetry may need redaction, summarization, or access controls before they enter an AI workflow.

11
00:01:27.563 --> 00:01:33.790
The more sensitive the source data, the more important it is to document what was shared and why.

12
00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:38.772
Evidence freshness matters because threat activity and reporting change.

13
00:01:38.772 --> 00:01:42.041
An infrastructure indicator may expire quickly.

14
00:01:42.041 --> 00:01:44.376
A public actor label may be revised.

15
00:01:44.376 --> 00:01:47.878
A campaign summary may be superseded by new evidence.

16
00:01:47.878 --> 00:01:54.260
AI can help summarize and compare sources, but it should not treat old reporting as current truth.

17
00:01:54.260 --> 00:02:05.235
Good preparation includes dates, source types, confidence notes, and caveats so the model and the analyst can distinguish current evidence from historical context.
